1
00:00:02,912 --> 00:00:06,974
Today, the Coca-Cola system sells
more than thirty-three billion

2
00:00:06,974 --> 00:00:10,675
cases of drinks a year, in over
two hundred countries and

3
00:00:10,675 --> 00:00:15,550
territories. In 2024, the
company's revenue was about

4
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,955
forty-seven billion dollars.

5
00:00:17,955 --> 00:00:21,017
And it still works a lot
like Candler's deal.

6
00:00:21,017 --> 00:00:24,992
The company mostly makes the
concentrate and builds the brand.

7
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:28,405
Independent bottling partners turn
it into drinks and get them

8
00:00:28,405 --> 00:00:29,757
to stores.

9
00:00:29,757 --> 00:00:32,932
Look back at the whole story, and
the recipe was never the whole

10
00:00:32,932 --> 00:00:36,470
secret. Free samples got people to try it.

11
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:39,544
A one-dollar deal put it in every town.

12
00:00:39,544 --> 00:00:41,695
A bottle made it hard to fake.

13
00:00:41,695 --> 00:00:44,057
A war carried it around the world.

14
00:00:44,057 --> 00:00:47,157
And when the company tried to
change it, its own customers

15
00:00:47,157 --> 00:00:48,523
wouldn't let it.

16
00:00:48,523 --> 00:00:51,773
John Pemberton sold about
nine glasses a day.

17
00:00:51,773 --> 00:00:53,623
He thought he'd made a medicine.

18
00:00:53,623 --> 00:00:56,098
What he actually started was a habit...

19
00:00:56,098 --> 00:01:00,073
repeated two point two
billion times a day.
